Blueprint for an AI bill of rights. Making automated systems work for the american people. https://www.whitehouse.gov/ostp/ai-bill-of-rights/ URL. Accessed. [ Google Scholar ] 32. Cohen JE. Knight First Amendment Institute at Columbia University; 2021. [26-01-2022]. How (not) to write a privacy law. https://knightcolumbia.org/content/how-not-to-write-a-privacy-law URL. Accessed. [ Google Scholar ] 33. Schmit C, Larson B, Kum HC. Data privacy in the time of plague. Yale J Health Policy Law Ethics. 2022;21:152–227. doi: 10.2139/ssrn.3968130. doi. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Lee LM. A bridge back to the future: public health ethics, bioethics, and environmental ethics. Am J Bioeth. 2017 Sep;17(9):5–12. doi: 10.1080/15265161.2017.1353164. doi. Medline. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. Schmit C, Ferdinand AO, Giannouchos T, Kum HC. Case study on communicating with research ethics committees about minimizing risk through software: an application for record linkage in secondary data analysis. JAMIA Open. 2024 Apr;7(1):ae010. doi: 10.1093/jamiaopen/ooae010. doi. Medline. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 36. World Health Organization . Official Records of the World Health Organization; 1948. [06-09-2024]. WHO definition of health. Preamble to the constitution of the world health organization. http://apps.who.int/gb/bd/PDF/bd47/EN/constitution-en.pdf?ua=1 URL. Accessed. [ Google Scholar ] 37. One health. Centers of Disease Control and Prevention. 2023. [20-06-2023]. https://www.cdc.gov/onehealth/index.html URL. Accessed. 38. Schmit C, Larson BN, Kum HC, et al. Public health informatics depends on engagement with privacy legislation. Health Aff Front. 2022 doi: 10.1377/FOREFRONT.20221027.571505. doi. [ DOI ] [ Google Scholar ] 39. World Health Organization Regulatory considerations on artificial intelligence for health. [02-02-2024];2023 https://iris.who.int/handle/10665/373421 URL. Accessed. 40. United Nations Members of the high-level AI